## 1. Goal‑model tables  

| **Name** | **Text** | **Runtime** | **Goal Type** | **Target Condition / Enquired Info** | **Relation** | **Justification** |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| **G1 – Deliver Requested Resources** | Deliver all requested resources to the specified location for the requesting agent. | `;` (sequential) | Achieve | *All requested resources are at the specified location and delivered to the requesting agent.* | AND | The mission can only finish when the collection phase finishes **and** the delivery phase finishes, and the two phases must occur in order. |
| **G2 – Perform Collection Phase** | Collect the requested resources from the designated storage locations. | `FALLBACK(G2.1, G4)` | Perform | – | AND | The collection phase may fail because the robot’s battery drops below 10 %. In that case the fallback child `G4` is executed. |
| **G2.1 – Collection Execution** | Execute the collection steps: plan order, navigate to storage, request resources, wait for retrieval. | `;` | Perform | – | AND | These four sub‑steps must be performed in the given order. |
| **G4 – Reassign Mission (Collection)** | Return to recharging station and assign mission to another robot when battery <10 % during collection. | `;` | Perform | – | AND | This is the alternative action when the collection phase fails due to low battery. |
| **G3 – Perform Delivery Phase** | Deliver collected resources to the specified destination. | `FALLBACK(G3.1, G5)` | Perform | – | AND | Delivery may fail because the robot’s battery drops below 30 %; the fallback child `G5` handles this. |
| **G3.1 – Delivery Execution** | Transport the collected resources to the destination. | `-` (leaf) | Perform | – | AND | A single action that completes the delivery phase. |
| **G5 – Reassign Mission (Delivery)** | Return resource to checkpoint and assign remaining task to another robot when battery <30 % during delivery. | `AND` | Perform | – | AND | Both returning and re‑assignment must happen. |
| **G5.1 – Return to Checkpoint** | Return the resource to the checkpoint before reassigning. | `FALLBACK(AT10, G5.2)` | Perform | – | AND | If the return fails, the alert child `G5.2` is executed. |
| **G5.2 – Trigger Alert** | Send alert and report to sector manager if returning to checkpoint fails. | `-` | Perform | – | AND | Handles the failure case of `G5.1`. |
| **G5.3 – Assign Remaining Task** | Assign the remaining delivery task to another robot after checkpoint return. | `-` | Perform | – | AND | Continues the mission once the resource is safely checkpointed. |

